  "reasoning": "The patient presents with chronic chest/epigastric pain, nausea, and significant anxiety. Reviewing the clinical patterns, persistent upper abdominal or chest discomfort paired with nausea and marked anxiety or worry is a classic presentation of peptic ulcer disease. The psychological distress (anxiety) often exacerbates gastrointestinal symptoms, and the chronic nature of the pain aligns with ulcer pathology. Other conditions like hypertension typically present with headaches and dizziness, while GERD focuses more on positional triggers and sour taste/belching. Therefore, peptic ulcer disease is the most consistent diagnosis.",
  "final_answer": "[DIAGNOSIS]peptic ulcer disease[/DIAGNOSIS]"
